From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CompSciOrBust <54033033+CompSciOrBust@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kern: run on the cores the machine has, up to four

The kernel started cores 1-3 unconditionally and then waited for all
four (cpu::NumCores) at every SynchronizeAllCores, so a machine with
fewer than four CPUs hung at boot.  On the generic-aarch64 board:

- TurnOnAllCores starts cores 1, 2, ... up to the CPU count the firmware
  reports (ACPI MADT, via the boot parameters; four if it gives none,
  never more than four) with the board's TryCpuOn, which checks the PSCI
  result.  The first core that fails to start ends the list.  Core 0
  then fixes the number of present cores and the board's core map, and
  only then lets the started cores into HorizonKernelMain.

- cpu::GetNumPresentCores() and GetPresentCoreMask() (kern_cpu.hpp) give
  that number.  Every place that iterates over, waits for, signals or
  places a thread on "all cores" uses them instead of NumCores:
  SynchronizeAllCores, DoOnEachCoreInOrder, the cache-maintenance IPIs,
  the scheduler's per-core loop, KDpcManager (requests, rotation, which
  core runs the preemption thread), the exit worker's core, interrupt
  unbinding, thread termination and debug "current on any core" loops,
  and the debugger-break thread list (absent cores report no thread).
  NumCores remains the size of every per-core array.  On other boards
  the two functions are constexpr and return NumCores, so their code is
  unchanged.

- Userland's virtual cores 0-3 and 63 are folded onto the present cores
  by the board's VirtualToPhysicalCoreMap, now set at boot (system core
  3 and 63 on the last core, applications on the others); so
  ConvertVirtualCoreMaskToPhysical is no longer constexpr on this board,
  and KCapabilities computes the initial processes' physical mask at run
  time.  Kernel threads name physical cores and no longer go through
  the map.  svcGetCurrentProcessorNumber returns the lowest virtual core
  in the thread's affinity mask that maps to the core it is running on,
  and svcGetInfo(IdleTickCount) takes a virtual core.  With four cores
  the map is the identity and both give the answers they gave before.

Other boards are unchanged.

---
diff --git a/libraries/libmesosphere/include/mesosphere/arch/arm64/kern_cpu.hpp b/libraries/libmesosphere/include/mesosphere/arch/arm64/kern_cpu.hpp
index c58b71b..bd47109 100644
--- a/libraries/libmesosphere/include/mesosphere/arch/arm64/kern_cpu.hpp
+++ b/libraries/libmesosphere/include/mesosphere/arch/arm64/kern_cpu.hpp
@@ -38,6 +38,32 @@ namespace ams::kern::arch::arm64::cpu {
     #error "Unknown Board for cpu::NumCores"
 #endif
 
+    /* NumCores is how many cores the kernel is built for: the size of every per-core array. */
+    /* GetNumPresentCores() is how many of them run, as physical cores 0 to n - 1; the kernel */
+    /* must not wait for, signal or schedule on any other. */
+#if defined(ATMOSPHERE_BOARD_GENERIC_AARCH64)
+    /* This board runs on however many cores the machine has, up to NumCores. The count is set */
+    /* once, on core 0, before the other cores reach HorizonKernelMain, and is constant */
+    /* afterwards. Defined, with the board's core map, in kern_cpu_map.cpp. */
+    extern constinit s32 g_num_present_cores;
+
+    ALWAYS_INLINE size_t GetNumPresentCores() {
+        return static_cast<size_t>(g_num_present_cores);
+    }
+
+    ALWAYS_INLINE u64 GetPresentCoreMask() {
+        return (1ul << GetNumPresentCores()) - 1ul;
+    }
+#else
+    constexpr ALWAYS_INLINE size_t GetNumPresentCores() {
+        return NumCores;
+    }
+
+    constexpr ALWAYS_INLINE u64 GetPresentCoreMask() {
+        return (1ul << NumCores) - 1ul;
+    }
+#endif
+
     constexpr inline u32 El0Aarch64PsrMask = 0xF0000000;
     constexpr inline u32 El0Aarch32PsrMask = 0xFE0FFE20;
 
